{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat it, in order that it may go well with you and with your children after you.</b> It specifies here 'and with your children after you,' because the commentators said that blood produces cruelty in the body of the one who eats it, and the nature of the father is drawn down also to the children, and their offspring will be like their source. Therefore it said: when you do not eat the blood, it will go well with you and with your children after you — so that the cruelty will not become an ingrained trait clinging to his seed. And therefore, nearby, in the destruction of the seduced city — young children and women on a single day — a great cruelty is seen, and one may fear lest the cruelty become an ingrained trait clinging to him and to his seed; therefore it said: ״וְנָתַן לְךָ רַחֲמִים״ — that you will be merciful by nature in any case toward all creatures, and through this cause HaShem will have mercy upon you. And this is what it said: ״וְנָתַן לְךָ רַחֲמִים וְרִחַמְךָ וְהִרְבֶּךָ״ — that is, that He will multiply your seed, for they too will be merciful like you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:12:11.649516793Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}